  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "An angry orange orb chased two police cruisers at midnight. In January 1975, patrolmen in Mansfield, Massachusetts watched a blazing light lock onto their vehicles.",
        "visual_query": "police cruiser night road massachusetts",
        "visual_fallback": "police car night driving"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The silent object hovered just feet above the roof, glowing with enough heat to warp the paint. When the cruiser accelerated to ninety miles an hour, the light matched every turn.",
        "visual_query": "glowing amber light night sky",
        "visual_fallback": "bright light dark sky"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Radio dispatchers listened in sheer panic as officers screamed for backup from a phantom pursuer. Civil defense radar confirmed an unlisted target tracking them from the clouds.",
        "visual_query": "vintage police radio equipment",
        "visual_fallback": "old radio console"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Decades of speculation dissolved when atmospheric physicists solved the chase. The cruisers had driven directly beneath high-voltage power lines during a rare ice storm, generating localized ball lightning.",
        "visual_query": "power lines winter storm night",
        "visual_fallback": "electric power lines snow"
      },
      {
        "narration": "A floating bubble of supercharged air acted like a living shadow. Could glowing air really mimic an intelligent pursuer?",
        "visual_query": "atmospheric plasma ball lightning",
        "visual_fallback": "glowing electric discharge"
      }
    ],
